@*
    "Håll skärmen vaken" — opt-in Screen Wake Lock toggle.

    A screen that sleeps mid-pass is a real problem on the day: the station pad locks while a
    shooter is halfway through a series, and a patrol list or live board on a monitor goes black
    with nobody near it to wake it. The lock is deliberately OPT-IN — holding a phone awake
    unasked drains a battery that has to last the whole competition (see the
    station-device-battery-cellular-constraint note).

    Why a partial: this exact toggle had already been hand-copied onto three screens
    (SpringskytteStarter, SpringskytteResultsManagement, FaltskytteStartledare), each with its own
    variable prefix. Three more screens needed it, and six copies of a browser-API dance with a
    visibilitychange re-acquire is how one of them ends up subtly wrong. Those three still carry
    their own copies — this is the one to converge on.

    Usage:
        @await Html.PartialAsync("_ScreenWakeButton")
        @await Html.PartialAsync("_ScreenWakeButton", new ViewDataDictionary(ViewData) {
            { "cssClass", "btn btn-outline-light btn-sm" } })

    Self-contained and instance-safe: the id is unique per render and the script is an IIFE, so
    two of these on one page cannot fight over the same lock.

    ⚠️ The OS releases the lock whenever the tab is hidden, so it MUST be re-acquired on
    visibilitychange — without that the toggle looks on and does nothing after the first
    tab switch. That is the bug this partial exists to stop being re-introduced.
*@
@{
    var wakeId = "wake_" + Guid.NewGuid().ToString("N").Substring(0, 8);
    var wakeCss = ViewData["cssClass"] as string ?? "btn btn-outline-secondary btn-sm";
}
<button type="button" id="@wakeId" class="@wakeCss" aria-pressed="false" title="Hindra skärmen från att slockna">
    <i class="bi bi-display me-1"></i>Håll skärmen vaken
</button>
<script>
(function () {
    var btn = document.getElementById('@wakeId');
    if (!btn) return;

    var lock = null;
    // Intent, kept separately from the lock itself: the lock object disappears on its own every
    // time the tab is hidden, so it cannot answer "does the operator still want this on".
    var wanted = false;

    function render() {
        btn.innerHTML = wanted
            ? '<i class="bi bi-display-fill me-1"></i>Skärm vaken'
            : '<i class="bi bi-display me-1"></i>Håll skärmen vaken';
        // Show state with .active + aria-pressed rather than by swapping in a specific Bootstrap
        // variant. The caller picks the variant (the dark live board passes btn-outline-light), and
        // forcing btn-secondary/btn-outline-secondary here would stack two variants on the same
        // button and let whichever rule came last in the stylesheet decide how it looks.
        btn.classList.toggle('active', wanted);
        btn.setAttribute('aria-pressed', wanted ? 'true' : 'false');
    }

    async function acquire() {
        if (!('wakeLock' in navigator)) return false;
        try {
            lock = await navigator.wakeLock.request('screen');
            lock.addEventListener('release', function () { lock = null; });
            return true;
        } catch (e) {
            // Best-effort by design: a denied or unsupported lock must never break the screen
            // it is sitting on. The button stays honest about what happened.
            return false;
        }
    }

    btn.addEventListener('click', async function () {
        if (wanted) {
            wanted = false;
            if (lock) { try { await lock.release(); } catch (e) { } lock = null; }
            render();
            return;
        }
        if (!('wakeLock' in navigator)) {
            // Say so rather than leaving a toggle that looks on and does nothing.
            btn.innerHTML = '<i class="bi bi-x me-1"></i>Stöds ej';
            return;
        }
        wanted = true;
        await acquire();
        render();
    });

    document.addEventListener('visibilitychange', async function () {
        if (wanted && !lock && document.visibilityState === 'visible') await acquire();
    });

    render();
})();
</script>
